 "customerTurns": 3,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hi, my Bosch WAN28281GB has stopped half way through a wash and is showing E18. Water still in the drum. What does that mean?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Before you start, switch it off and unplug it. E18 on your Bosch means: No drainage / drain took too long (clogged coin-trap/pump filter or drain hose). From what you have described, the most likely cause is blocked pump filter / foreign object in the pump path. The most common cause is a blockage in the pump filter (also called the drain filter or trap), and it's a free fix. On most washing machines it's behind a small flap or kick-plate at the bottom front. Could you check the filter and tell me what you find — was it clear, did you find and remove something, is there a blockage you can't shift, or does anything look broken?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks. I've unscrewed the filter and found a child's sock and a hair grip wrapped round it, plus a lot of fluff. I had to empty the water out first with the little emergency hose and a baking tray, and the floor got a little wet. What should I do now?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Clear any remaining debris from the filter housing and ensure the drain pump impeller spins freely. Reset the machine by turning it off, waiting a few minutes, and then starting a new cycle to see if the error clears. Now that the blockage is cleared, let's test it: run a drain or spin-only programme. Does the water pump away now?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I've cleaned the filter and checked the impeller by hand (power off) - it turns, slightly notchy then free. I ran a rinse & spin and it drains quickly now, E18 has gone and it spins normally. Is there anything else I should do?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
